      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "The three CMIP6 models are to be used on their own native grids, and this fragment matters because the archive grid labels and the fact that GFDL-ESM4 output is regridded while CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are native affect how the Niño 3.4 area mask and cell areas are applied.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use each source on its own archived grid for the Niño 3.4 regional mean; note that GFDL-ESM4 is `gr` (already regridded to a 1° archive grid), while CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are `gn`.",
        "Because the task is a regional average/index, not a budget or map-to-map statistic, compute on each source’s own published grid and own cell areas rather than forcing a common grid."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
